00:05:01.632 --> 00:05:04.932
One design pays only if a side gets more votes than the other.

00:05:05.492 --> 00:05:08.352
The price on that contract is a chance of finishing ahead.

00:05:08.352 --> 00:05:12.892
the other design pays with the share of the popular vote, so its price is a

00:05:12.892 --> 00:05:18.012
margin, not a winner. A paper in P.S. political science and politics read both

00:05:18.012 --> 00:05:24.272
for the 2024 popular vote on September 29th. The vote share book was thin and it

00:05:24.272 --> 00:05:28.932
put the Democratic margin at 9 percentage points. The winner takes all book was

00:05:28.932 --> 00:05:34.592
thick and it put the chance the Democrat would get more votes at 85.7%. The

00:05:34.592 --> 00:05:37.012
The authors mixed the two books into one distribution.

00:05:37.592 --> 00:05:42.212
The margin came down to six or seven points, and the chance of finishing ahead moved up

00:05:42.212 --> 00:05:43.552
to 87%.

00:05:43.872 --> 00:05:46.032
They still said a lot of uncertainty was left.

00:05:46.692 --> 00:05:48.092
Walk the three numbers in order.

00:05:48.472 --> 00:05:52.492
Nine points is a priced margin from a thin book, not a win probability.

00:05:53.272 --> 00:05:57.352
85.7% is a chance of finishing ahead, not a margin.

00:05:57.952 --> 00:06:00.792
The blend is a smaller margin and a slightly higher chance.

00:06:00.792 --> 00:06:00.952
stance.

